<title>SOUTH KOREA: LG wins $42 mln Libyan aircon deal.</title>
<headline>LG wins $42 mln Libyan aircon deal.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's LG Electronics Inc said on Tuesday it has agreed to supply $42 million worth of air conditioners to Libya's state-run electric power firm Arab Co For Engineering Industries over the next three years.</p>
<p>LG Electronics, a unit of LG Group, said in a statement it would ship a total of 36,000 air conditioners, beginning from early next year.</p>
<p>It said LG also planned to transfer air conditioner production technology to the Libyan company.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newroom (822) 727 5643</p>
